0
00:00:07,179 --> 00:00:10,214
♪♪♪

1
00:00:10,214 --> 00:00:11,817
THE LIFE OF A TOP MODEL

2
00:00:11,817 --> 00:00:13,385
IS THE STUFF OF DREAMS.

3
00:00:13,385 --> 00:00:16,221
YOUNG GIRLS EVERYWHERE
FANTASIZE ABOUT THE GLITZ,

4
00:00:16,221 --> 00:00:17,589
THE GLAMOUR,

5
00:00:17,589 --> 00:00:19,524
AND THE GOAL OF TRANSFORMING
FROM AWKWARD TEENS

6
00:00:19,524 --> 00:00:21,893
TO RUNWAY IDOLS.

7
00:00:21,893 --> 00:00:24,362
AND THEY'RE ALL WAITING
FOR THEIR BIG BREAK.

8
00:00:24,362 --> 00:00:25,597
I CAN WIN,
I KNOW IT.

9
00:00:25,597 --> 00:00:26,898
I'M GONNA BLOW
EVERYBODY AWAY.

10
00:00:26,898 --> 00:00:28,300
AMERICA'S
NEXT TOP MODEL.

11
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,868
STAY TUNED.

12
00:00:29,868 --> 00:00:32,637
FOR OUR SIXTH CYCLE OF
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,"

13
00:00:32,637 --> 00:00:36,508
I GAVE 32 PROMISING GIRLS A
CHANCE TO FLY TO LOS ANGELES

14
00:00:36,508 --> 00:00:40,779
AND PROVE THEY HAD TOP MODEL
POTENTIAL.

15
00:00:40,779 --> 00:00:41,880
WE MADE THEM WALK.

16
00:00:44,883 --> 00:00:45,884
TALK.

17
00:00:45,884 --> 00:00:47,385
I KNOW I'M PRETTY,
YOU KNOW,

18
00:00:47,385 --> 00:00:49,454
I HEAR IT ENOUGH THAT IT'S JUST
ABSOLUTELY RIDICULOUS

19
00:00:49,454 --> 00:00:50,822
WHY I'M NOT
A SUPERMODEL.

20
00:00:50,822 --> 00:00:52,491
IF YOU'RE GONNA ASK ME TO GET
DOWN AND STRIP NAKED,

21
00:00:52,491 --> 00:00:53,492
I WILL DO IT.

22
00:00:53,492 --> 00:00:54,493
WELL?

23
00:00:54,493 --> 00:00:55,794
BUT THE THING IS,
LIKE,

24
00:00:55,794 --> 00:00:57,662
MY PARENTS KIND OF HAVE A THING
WITH THAT.

25
00:00:57,662 --> 00:00:59,297
STRIP AWAY THEIR FAÇADES.

26
00:00:59,297 --> 00:01:01,500
I DID SOME AMATEUR NIGHTS AT
STRIP CLUBS, LIKE, FOR MONEY.

27
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,968
AND SHOW ME
THEIR TRUE SELVES.

28
00:01:02,968 --> 00:01:04,836
I DID NOT COME
ALL THE WAY

29
00:01:04,836 --> 00:01:06,505
FROM LITTLE BITTY
LITTLE ROCK, ARKANSAS

30
00:01:06,505 --> 00:01:07,739
TO GET TURNED AROUND
AND GO HOME,

31
00:01:07,739 --> 00:01:08,807
THAT'S NOT
AN OPTION.

32
00:01:08,807 --> 00:01:10,274
I'M A REAL
LIVE--

33
00:01:10,274 --> 00:01:11,743
I KEEP CHARGING
TILL I GET WHAT I WANT

34
00:01:11,743 --> 00:01:13,912
AND I WANT THIS
RIGHT HERE.

35
00:01:13,912 --> 00:01:15,280
I'M NOT PLAYING!

36
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,948
WE MADE IT!
(screaming)

37
00:01:16,948 --> 00:01:18,550
IN THE END,

38
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:21,219
I CHOSE 13 GIRLS TO MOVE
INTO THE TOP MODEL HOUSE

39
00:01:21,219 --> 00:01:23,922
AND COMPETE
FOR THEIR ULTIMATE DREAM.

40
00:01:23,922 --> 00:01:26,191
NOW ONLY FIVE GIRLS
REMAIN.

41
00:01:26,191 --> 00:01:27,259
JADE.

42
00:01:27,259 --> 00:01:27,859
FURONDA.

43
00:01:27,859 --> 00:01:29,294
JOANIE.

44
00:01:29,294 --> 00:01:30,495
DANIELLE.

45
00:01:30,495 --> 00:01:31,329
AND SARA.

46
00:01:32,397 --> 00:01:34,933
TONIGHT, SEE HOW
IT ALL WENT DOWN.

47
00:01:34,933 --> 00:01:38,537
THIS IS NOT "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP
BEST FRIEND."

48
00:01:38,537 --> 00:01:40,405
PLUS, NEVER-BEFORE-SEEN
MODEL MOMENTS,

49
00:01:40,405 --> 00:01:41,940
INCLUDING CLASSIC ADVICE

50
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,875
FROM OUR FAVORITE CLASSIC
SUPERMODEL.

51
00:01:43,875 --> 00:01:45,377
YOU, OUT OF
ALL THE GIRLS,

52
00:01:45,377 --> 00:01:46,945
YOU'VE GOT TO GROOM YOURSELF
A LITTLE BIT MORE.

53
00:01:46,945 --> 00:01:49,614
AND AN UNUSUAL APPROACH TO
BONDING.

54
00:01:49,614 --> 00:01:50,849
(crunching)
OW, GINA!

55
00:01:52,417 --> 00:01:54,452
♪ WANNA BE ON TOP ♪

56
00:02:03,461 --> 00:02:05,330
THE COMPETITION WAS
OFF AND RUNNING

57
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:08,834
WHEN THE TOP 13 MOVED INTO
THEIR LUSH L.A. MANSION.

58
00:02:08,834 --> 00:02:11,469
(girls shouting)

59
00:02:16,842 --> 00:02:20,278
THIS IS DEFINITELY THE CRAZIEST,
MOST BEAUTIFUL HOUSE

60
00:02:20,278 --> 00:02:22,414
I'VE EVER BEEN IN.

61
00:02:22,414 --> 00:02:24,216
YOU HAD
THE IMAN ROOM,

62
00:02:24,216 --> 00:02:25,417
YOU HAD
TWIGGY'S ROOM,

63
00:02:25,417 --> 00:02:27,452
WE HAD
JANICE'S ROOM.

64
00:02:27,452 --> 00:02:28,520
NIGEL,
I WAS LIKE,

65
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:29,521
I NEVER KNEW
HE WAS A MODEL.

66
00:02:29,521 --> 00:02:31,223
THAT WAS BAD--
HE'S IN THERE!

67
00:02:31,223 --> 00:02:31,756
I KNOW,
I SAW HIM,

68
00:02:31,756 --> 00:02:32,791
HE LOOKED HOT.

69
00:02:33,491 --> 00:02:34,526
HE'S HOT.

70
00:02:34,526 --> 00:02:35,894
HE STILL
IS HOT.

71
00:02:35,894 --> 00:02:37,729
OH, WE GOT
GUMBALLS!

72
00:02:39,364 --> 00:02:40,899
OH.

73
00:02:40,899 --> 00:02:44,569
FURONDA SETTLED INTO
THE HIGH LIFE WITH EASE.

74
00:02:44,569 --> 00:02:47,239
CONFIDENCE IS THE MAJOR FACTOR
IN MODELING.

75
00:02:47,239 --> 00:02:49,975
I'M THE PRINCESS AND THE QUEEN
OF THE HOUSE

76
00:02:49,975 --> 00:02:54,479
AND I JUST HAVE TO LET THE GIRLS
KNOW THAT I'M SO SPECIAL.

77
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:57,282
I LIKE HOW HER TIARA,
LIKE, IS NOT COMING OFF.

78
00:02:57,282 --> 00:02:58,817
THIS IS UNREAL.

79
00:02:58,817 --> 00:03:00,418
FURONDA PUTS ON HER LITTLE,
LIKE, TIARA CROWN.

80
00:03:00,418 --> 00:03:01,753
I'M LIKE,
WHO DOES THAT?

81
00:03:01,753 --> 00:03:03,555
IT JUST SEEMS A LITTLE TACKY
AND FAKE TO ME.

82
00:03:03,555 --> 00:03:06,258
WHILE SOUTHERN BELLE KATHY
WAS WIDE-EYED.

83
00:03:06,258 --> 00:03:07,792
I CANNOT BELIEVE THIS.

84
00:03:07,792 --> 00:03:11,196
THIS IS, LIKE, THE TEMPLE OF
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

85
00:03:11,196 --> 00:03:12,731
MY FOLKS
DON'T REALLY GET

86
00:03:12,731 --> 00:03:14,966
THE WHOLE "GOING OFF TO
HOLLYWOOD TO BECOME A MODEL"

87
00:03:14,966 --> 00:03:19,537
BECAUSE THEY ALMOST WANT ME
TO KIND OF STAY AT HOME

88
00:03:19,537 --> 00:03:20,839
AND BE
A HOUSEWIFE.

89
00:03:20,839 --> 00:03:22,240
CHICKEN NOODLE!

90
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,241
IT'S MY FAVORITE!

91
00:03:23,241 --> 00:03:24,242
CHICKEN
AND NOODLE.

92
00:03:24,242 --> 00:03:25,377
IT'S MY FAVORITE.

93
00:03:25,377 --> 00:03:27,679
BUT HOW MANY PEOPLE IN THE WORLD
GET TO DO THIS?

94
00:03:27,679 --> 00:03:29,414
IT'S LIKE GOING
TO THE MOON.

95
00:03:32,350 --> 00:03:34,319
BUT THE VERY FIRST
PHOTO SHOOT,

96
00:03:34,319 --> 00:03:36,288
WE DIDN'T WANT THE GIRLS TO BE
ABLE TO PLAY IT SAFE.

97
00:03:36,288 --> 00:03:37,923
SO WE WENT
TO THE EXTREME

98
00:03:37,923 --> 00:03:41,493
AND GAVE THEM ABSOLUTELY
NOTHING TO HIDE BEHIND.

99
00:03:41,493 --> 00:03:43,929
THEY PAINTED OUR HEADS SO THAT
WE LOOKED BALD

100
00:03:43,929 --> 00:03:45,563
AND IT REALLY, REALLY LOOKED
LIKE WE WERE BALD.

101
00:03:45,563 --> 00:03:47,365
ARE YOU
THE DIVA?

102
00:03:47,365 --> 00:03:48,667
SUPPOSEDLY.

103
00:03:48,667 --> 00:03:51,336
I AM THE DIVA,
HOW'D YOU KNOW?

104
00:03:51,336 --> 00:03:53,638
I THINK MY FACE
IS MY BEST ASSET.

105
00:03:53,638 --> 00:03:54,873
I'M READY TO GET
IN FRONT OF THE CAMERA,

106
00:03:54,873 --> 00:03:56,508
I'VE BEEN PRACTICING
IN THE MIRROR,

107
00:03:56,508 --> 00:03:57,943
SO I KNOW
I'M GONNA ROCK IT.

108
00:03:57,943 --> 00:04:00,512
SOME GIRLS DID ROCK IT
RIGHT OFF THE BAT.

109
00:04:00,512 --> 00:04:01,579
VERY NICE,
BEAUTIFUL.

110
00:04:03,315 --> 00:04:04,316
BEAUTIFUL.

111
00:04:04,316 --> 00:04:05,884
THAT'S REALLY
ELEGANT.

112
00:04:05,884 --> 00:04:07,752
THAT'S VERY NICE.

113
00:04:07,752 --> 00:04:09,854
HIGH-FIVE, 'CAUSE THIS--
THIS IS FIERCE.

114
00:04:11,323 --> 00:04:12,557
WHILE OTHER GIRLS,

115
00:04:12,557 --> 00:04:14,960
INCLUDING THE FEARLESS FURONDA,
STRUGGLED.

116
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,494
WHEN FURONDA GOT IN FRONT
OF THE CAMERA,

117
00:04:16,494 --> 00:04:18,430
SHE WAS
NOT ONLY AWKWARD,

118
00:04:18,430 --> 00:04:20,332
SHE REALLY DIDN'T
KNOW HER ANGLES.

119
00:04:20,332 --> 00:04:22,867
OOH!

120
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:25,770
I DO KIND OF FEEL LIKE
A PENIS WITH EARS.

121
00:04:25,770 --> 00:04:28,740
I'M WEARING A CONDOM ON MY HEAD,
A HUGE CONDOM.

122
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,709
LOWER YOUR HAND
A LITTLE BIT.

123
00:04:30,709 --> 00:04:32,577
I NEED A LITTLE MORE WARMTH
IN THE FACE.

124
00:04:32,577 --> 00:04:34,779
THINK OF SOMETHING THAT MAKES
YOU HAPPY.

125
00:04:34,779 --> 00:04:35,780
HAPPY?

126
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:37,415
HAPPY,
I'M HAPPY.

127
00:04:37,415 --> 00:04:38,850
MY BOYFRIEND.

128
00:04:38,850 --> 00:04:40,251
FLOWERS.

129
00:04:40,251 --> 00:04:43,588
WATER.

130
00:04:43,588 --> 00:04:44,689
I'M HAPPY.

131
00:04:46,424 --> 00:04:48,393
AT JUDGING,

132
00:04:48,393 --> 00:04:50,862
THE CONFIDENT FURONDA HAD THE
RUG PULLED OUT FROM UNDER HER.

133
00:04:50,862 --> 00:04:54,232
FURONDA, YOU THOUGHT
THAT YOU DID AN AMAZING JOB

134
00:04:54,232 --> 00:04:55,633
IN YOUR PHOTO SHOOT.

135
00:04:55,633 --> 00:04:57,702
SOME OF THE JUDGES
THINK YOU DID THE WORST.

136
00:04:57,702 --> 00:04:59,904
THE GIRL WITH THE WORST PHOTO
IN THE BUNCH.

137
00:04:59,904 --> 00:05:01,639
KATHY.

138
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:03,541
BUT WITH ALL OF KATHY'S
DOWN-HOME QUALITIES.

139
00:05:03,541 --> 00:05:05,243
YOU HAVE
TERRIBLE POSTURE.

140
00:05:05,243 --> 00:05:06,444
RELAX YOUR ARMS.

141
00:05:06,444 --> 00:05:07,946
BACK.

142
00:05:07,946 --> 00:05:10,815
"AHH."
AHH!

143
00:05:10,815 --> 00:05:13,518
THE JUDGES JUST COULDN'T
SEE A TOP MODEL IN HER.

144
00:05:13,518 --> 00:05:15,220
IT'S-- IT'S NOT
A MODEL'S FACE.

145
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:17,756
IN EVERY HOME TOWN, THERE ARE
GIRLS THAT LOOK LIKE KATHY.

146
00:05:17,756 --> 00:05:19,424
AND SHE WAS SENT HOME.

147
00:05:25,263 --> 00:05:27,565
COMING UP,
JADE GETS A SPELLING LESSON.

148
00:05:27,565 --> 00:05:28,767
HOW DO YOU SPELL "ET CETERA"?

149
00:05:28,767 --> 00:05:30,969
E-X-C-E-D-E-R-A.

150
00:05:30,969 --> 00:05:33,538
IS THAT WRONG?

151
00:05:33,538 --> 00:05:36,975
AND LATER, THE GIRLS THINK THE
JUDGES MADE A BIG MISTAKE.

152
00:05:36,975 --> 00:05:39,544
I'VE NEVER BEEN IN SO MUCH
SHOCK, I THINK.

153
00:05:44,649 --> 00:05:45,917
♪♪♪

154
00:05:49,454 --> 00:05:50,889
I WANT
A MOHAWK.

155
00:05:50,889 --> 00:05:52,223
WORD?

156
00:05:52,223 --> 00:05:53,258
I WANT THAT, WITH THE COLLARS
POPPED,

157
00:05:53,258 --> 00:05:54,692
THEY DID SOMETHING CRAZY.

158
00:05:54,692 --> 00:05:56,895
IT ALWAYS TURNS THE COMPETITION
UPSIDE-DOWN

159
00:05:56,895 --> 00:05:58,763
TO GIVE THE GIRLS
BRAND-NEW LOOKS,

160
00:05:58,763 --> 00:06:01,800
SO I SENT ALL OF THEM
TO THE SALON FOR A MAKEOVER.

161
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:03,868
OR JUST, LIKE, EXTENSIONS, LIKE,
THAT MATCH MY NATURAL HAIR

162
00:06:03,868 --> 00:06:05,937
OR I COULD DO
THE STRAIGHT THING,

163
00:06:05,937 --> 00:06:08,773
BUT I WANT, LIKE A--
LIKE A BRONZE COPPER.

164
00:06:08,773 --> 00:06:10,442
BUT ON MAKEOVER DAY,

165
00:06:10,442 --> 00:06:13,411
WHAT THE GIRLS WANT IS NOT
ALWAYS WHAT THE GIRLS GET.

166
00:06:13,411 --> 00:06:17,348
JADE, WE WANT TO MAKE YOU LOOK
SOFTER, SWEETER, ELFLIKE.

167
00:06:17,348 --> 00:06:21,553
THIS SHORT, BLONDISH,
WITH BLONDISH EYEBROWS.

168
00:06:21,553 --> 00:06:23,354
I WAS REALLY SHOCKED
ABOUT THAT.

169
00:06:23,354 --> 00:06:24,355
IT FREAKED ME
OUT.

170
00:06:24,355 --> 00:06:26,291
♪♪♪

171
00:06:26,291 --> 00:06:28,626
SOME GIRLS WERE THRILLED WITH
THEIR NEW LOOKS.

172
00:06:28,626 --> 00:06:30,428
THE HAIR IS JUST REALLY
VERSATILE,

173
00:06:30,428 --> 00:06:33,798
ENDED UP GIVING ME A LOT MORE
TO WORK WITH WITH MY LOOK.

174
00:06:33,798 --> 00:06:35,700
SOME JUST TRIED
TO PLAY ALONG.

175
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:37,602
TRY GETTING
MORE USED TO IT.

176
00:06:42,841 --> 00:06:43,508
WHY?

177
00:06:44,676 --> 00:06:46,578
AND JADE STARTED
TO UNRAVEL.

178
00:06:46,578 --> 00:06:48,813
I DON'T KNOW WHY THEY'RE LEAVING
MY TOP LONGER THAN MY SIDES.

179
00:06:48,813 --> 00:06:50,348
ANTONIO,
WAS LIKE,

180
00:06:50,348 --> 00:06:52,383
WE'RE GONNA CUT THIS SHORT
AND LEAVE THIS HIGH.

181
00:06:52,383 --> 00:06:53,751
I FEEL LIKE LENGTH
IS VERY IMPORTANT.

182
00:06:53,751 --> 00:06:55,487
IF YOU LOOK
AT ANY MAGAZINE,

183
00:06:55,487 --> 00:06:57,689
A LOT OF MODELS HAVE LONG,
"LENGTHLY" HAIR.

184
00:06:57,689 --> 00:07:00,225
LOOK, THIS IS
WHAT I SHOULD HAVE.

185
00:07:00,225 --> 00:07:01,659
DAMN IT.

186
00:07:01,659 --> 00:07:03,328
I GUESS THEY THOUGHT
I WAS JUST TOO CONFIDENT.

187
00:07:03,328 --> 00:07:04,462
I DON'T UNDERSTAND IT.

188
00:07:04,462 --> 00:07:05,864
FURONDA'S, LIKE,
MORE ARROGANT THAN YOU.

189
00:07:05,864 --> 00:07:07,765
YEAH, DUDE--
YOU THINK I'M ARROGANT?

190
00:07:07,765 --> 00:07:08,833
NO, I DIDN'T SAY--

191
00:07:08,833 --> 00:07:10,235
NO, NO, I SAID
MORE THAN

192
00:07:10,235 --> 00:07:11,569
I WOULD THINK YOU WOULD BE
CALLED OUT FIRST.

193
00:07:11,569 --> 00:07:12,837
I'M NOT ARROGANT.

194
00:07:12,837 --> 00:07:13,872
NO, NO, NO,
I DON'T THINK SO EITHER.

195
00:07:13,872 --> 00:07:15,473
I DIDN'T WANT TO EVEN
LOOK IN THE MIRROR

196
00:07:15,473 --> 00:07:17,976
'CAUSE I WAS STILL NOT ADJUSTED
TO THE WAY I LOOK.

197
00:07:17,976 --> 00:07:19,644
I DON'T EVEN LOOK
LIKE I BELONG ON THIS PLANET.

198
00:07:19,644 --> 00:07:21,412
FOR DANIELLE,

199
00:07:21,412 --> 00:07:23,681
THE HAIR ON HER HEAD WASN'T THE
ONLY THING THAT GOT REDONE.

200
00:07:23,681 --> 00:07:25,550
MINIMAL GROOMING
AROUND THE LIP

201
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:29,320
WILL HELP A WOMAN OUT
FROM LOOKING LIKE A MAN.

202
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:31,589
YOU TRYING TO SAY
I LOOK LIKE A MAN, MR. JAY?

203
00:07:31,589 --> 00:07:32,757
I DON'T THINK
YOU LOOK LIKE A MAN,

204
00:07:32,757 --> 00:07:34,792
BUT YOU DON'T WANNA
BE CONFUSED FOR-- SEE?

205
00:07:34,792 --> 00:07:36,294
NOT PRETTY.

206
00:07:36,294 --> 00:07:37,328
DOES IT HURT,
LIKE, REALLY BAD?

207
00:07:37,328 --> 00:07:38,730
NO.

208
00:07:38,730 --> 00:07:40,365
YOU TELLING
THE TRUTH?

209
00:07:43,968 --> 00:07:45,603
HOO.

210
00:07:48,206 --> 00:07:52,911
I HAVE BEEN COMPLETELY BUTCHED
ON THE SIDES.

211
00:07:52,911 --> 00:07:55,246
I'M TRYING MY BEST
TO GET USED TO IT,

212
00:07:55,246 --> 00:08:00,885
BUT THIS IS THE COMPLETE
OPPOSITE OF MY PERSONAL STYLE.

213
00:08:00,885 --> 00:08:03,188
I WAS SITTING THERE AND I WAS
LIKE, I AM NOT GONNA CRY,

214
00:08:03,188 --> 00:08:04,722
LIKE, I WILL NOT
BE THAT GIRL.

215
00:08:04,722 --> 00:08:06,191
And you're always gonna
be true to yourself.

216
00:08:06,191 --> 00:08:07,258
And you're
still there.

217
00:08:07,258 --> 00:08:08,259
You're still Sara.

218
00:08:08,259 --> 00:08:09,727
YEAH.

219
00:08:09,727 --> 00:08:11,362
I mean, your hair is just
a little different-- so what?

220
00:08:11,362 --> 00:08:12,931
In college, Sara,

221
00:08:12,931 --> 00:08:14,666
I shaved my head except for
two, little, like, horns.

222
00:08:16,968 --> 00:08:19,304
I mean, I know your hair
don't look that bad.

223
00:08:19,304 --> 00:08:20,705
ALTHOUGH SOME OF THE GIRLS
WEREN'T EXACTLY THRILLED

224
00:08:20,705 --> 00:08:22,307
WITH THEIR NEW LOOK,

225
00:08:22,307 --> 00:08:25,276
FURONDA WAS SO CALM AND
CONFIDENT WITH HER NEW HAIR

226
00:08:25,276 --> 00:08:27,478
THAT SHE DECIDED TO LET HER
ROOMMATES KNOW

227
00:08:27,478 --> 00:08:29,647
EXACTLY WHO WAS
IN CHARGE.

228
00:08:29,647 --> 00:08:31,349
I'M ABOUT
TO HAND OUT MY RULES.

229
00:08:31,349 --> 00:08:33,318
I'LL DO IT
IN MY FURONDA ACCENT.

230
00:08:33,318 --> 00:08:37,222
"IF YOU HAVE A PROBLEM WITH ANY
OF YOUR ACTIONS TOWARD ME,

231
00:08:37,222 --> 00:08:40,825
"I WILL FIND YOU AND TRY
TO RESOLVE THE PROBLEM.

232
00:08:40,825 --> 00:08:42,961
"FEEL FREE
TO DO THE SAME."

233
00:08:42,961 --> 00:08:45,430
(laughing)

234
00:08:45,430 --> 00:08:47,966
AND YOU SPELLED "ET CETERA"
WRONG, DING-DONG.

235
00:08:47,966 --> 00:08:49,601
HOW DO YOU SPELL
"ET CETERA"?

236
00:08:49,601 --> 00:08:52,570
E-X-C-E-D-E-R-A.

237
00:08:52,570 --> 00:08:53,905
IT TOOK ME A MINUTE,
YO?

238
00:08:53,905 --> 00:08:54,906
WAIT.

239
00:08:54,906 --> 00:08:57,275
E-X-C-E-D-E-A-R.

240
00:08:57,275 --> 00:08:58,676
"ET CETERA."

241
00:08:58,676 --> 00:09:00,211
(laughing)

242
00:09:00,211 --> 00:09:01,412
IS THAT WRONG?

243
00:09:01,412 --> 00:09:03,181
DID YOU, LIKE,
WRITE THIS BEFORE YOU CAME?

244
00:09:03,181 --> 00:09:04,549
WHAT IS
THIS ABOUT?

245
00:09:04,549 --> 00:09:06,417
TO MAKE RULES FOR EVERYBODY,
LIKE, WHAT IS THIS ABOUT?

246
00:09:06,417 --> 00:09:07,952
LADIES!

247
00:09:07,952 --> 00:09:09,821
HELLO.

248
00:09:09,821 --> 00:09:12,590
FURONDA'S TIPS HAD
ALL THE GIRLS TALKING.

249
00:09:12,590 --> 00:09:13,825
"NUMBER ONE.

250
00:09:13,825 --> 00:09:16,227
"I WILL RESPECT YOU AND
ALL OF YOUR BELONGINGS.

251
00:09:16,227 --> 00:09:17,829
"PLEASE SHOW ME THE SAME
COURTESY."

252
00:09:17,829 --> 00:09:19,664
ARE WE IN KINDERGARTEN
AGAIN?

253
00:09:19,664 --> 00:09:21,499
LIKE, FOR REAL,
FOR REAL?

254
00:09:21,499 --> 00:09:23,434
"NUMBER TWO,
IF YOU MUST DISCUSS ME,

255
00:09:23,434 --> 00:09:25,536
"I AM THE BEST PERSON
TO DISCUSS ME WITH."

256
00:09:25,536 --> 00:09:26,838
I HAD A COPY FOR YOU,

257
00:09:26,838 --> 00:09:27,872
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO GIVE HER YOURS.

258
00:09:27,872 --> 00:09:29,307
THIS IS
COMMON KNOWLEDGE.

259
00:09:29,307 --> 00:09:31,376
LIKE, THIS IS
JUST PATRONIZING.

260
00:09:31,376 --> 00:09:32,577
IF YOU WANNA
THROW IT AWAY,

261
00:09:32,577 --> 00:09:34,545
YOU CAN THROW IT AWAY,
BUT I GAVE IT TO YOU.

262
00:09:34,545 --> 00:09:37,282
EVERY GIRL HAS TO MAKE
SACRIFICES TO COMPETE.

263
00:09:37,282 --> 00:09:38,883
BUT WHEN WENDY CAME
TO "TOP MODEL",

264
00:09:38,883 --> 00:09:41,853
SHE LEFT BEHIND
A LIFE IN TURMOIL.

265
00:09:41,853 --> 00:09:44,255
I WANT TO ASK YOU ABOUT NEW
ORLEANS AND HURRICANE KATRINA.

266
00:09:44,255 --> 00:09:47,358
I'M SLOWLY GETTING OVER
EVERYTHING FROM NEW ORLEANS.

267
00:09:47,358 --> 00:09:49,193
I DIDN'T KNOW
WHERE MY PARENTS WERE.

268
00:09:49,193 --> 00:09:50,561
THEY WERE TRYING
TO EVACUATE

269
00:09:50,561 --> 00:09:52,797
AND THEY JUST SLEPT IN A CAR
FOR, LIKE, TWO DAYS

270
00:09:52,797 --> 00:09:55,400
AND THAT WAS THE LAST TIME
I TALKED TO 'EM.

271
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,234
(crying)
SORRY.

272
00:09:58,436 --> 00:10:00,204
I DIDN'T KNOW
WHERE MY PARENTS WERE

273
00:10:00,204 --> 00:10:03,374
AND THEN FINALLY,
WE GOT IN TOUCH.

274
00:10:03,374 --> 00:10:06,411
We had, like, eight-and-a-half
feet of water in the house.

275
00:10:06,411 --> 00:10:07,679
You couldn't walk anywhere

276
00:10:07,679 --> 00:10:10,882
because that muddy,
sludgy stuff?

277
00:10:10,882 --> 00:10:13,885
That's, like,
maybe five inches thick.

278
00:10:13,885 --> 00:10:16,254
AND JADE STRUGGLED
TO KEEP IT TOGETHER.

279
00:10:16,254 --> 00:10:17,655
YO, I NEED
TO USE THE PHONE.

280
00:10:17,655 --> 00:10:19,424
I HAVE NOT USED THE PHONE,
LIKE, SINCE I GOT MY HAIR CUT.

281
00:10:19,424 --> 00:10:20,458
MAY I PLEASE USE
THE PHONE?

282
00:10:20,458 --> 00:10:21,592
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

283
00:10:21,592 --> 00:10:22,727
WELL, GIVE ME A TIME,
THEN, PLEASE.

284
00:10:22,727 --> 00:10:23,961
I HAD TO GET UP
AT 3:00 IN THE MORNING.

285
00:10:23,961 --> 00:10:25,396
I HADN'T TALKED TO MY FAMILY
SINCE MY MAKEOVER,

286
00:10:25,396 --> 00:10:26,798
SO EVERYTHING WAS BUILDING UP
INSIDE OF ME.

287
00:10:26,798 --> 00:10:29,300
YO, I'M TIRED
OF STRUGGLING.

288
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:31,502
I FEEL LIKE I AM THE
UNDISCOVERED SUPERMODEL,

289
00:10:31,502 --> 00:10:32,837
YOU KNOW
WHAT I'M SAYING?

290
00:10:32,837 --> 00:10:35,373
I LIVE IN NEW YORK CITY,
THE BELLY OF THE BEAST.

291
00:10:35,373 --> 00:10:37,408
I'M TIRED
OF THIS.

292
00:10:37,408 --> 00:10:40,345
SHE'S NOT FROM THIS PLANET,
SO SHE SAYS.

293
00:10:40,345 --> 00:10:42,447
AND YOU KNOW WHAT?

294
00:10:42,447 --> 00:10:44,248
I THINK
I BELIEVE IT.

295
00:10:44,248 --> 00:10:45,917
THIS IS UGLY.

296
00:10:45,917 --> 00:10:47,452
AND THIS IS WHAT I SAID IN THE
CAR AND I'VE BEEN SAYING THIS,

297
00:10:47,452 --> 00:10:48,486
THIS IS
GONNA GET UGLY.

298
00:10:48,486 --> 00:10:49,921
THIS IS
A COMPETITION.

299
00:10:49,921 --> 00:10:53,257
THIS IS NOT "AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP BEST FRIEND."

300
00:10:53,257 --> 00:10:56,227
MAYBE SHE'S BIPOLAR
OR SOMETHING,

301
00:10:56,227 --> 00:10:58,429
BECAUSE THE BEHAVIOR
THAT SHE DISPLAYED

302
00:10:58,429 --> 00:11:00,465
WAS JUST
TOTALLY ERRATIC.

303
00:11:00,465 --> 00:11:02,600
I AM BLONDE,
I AM SHORT.

304
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,736
I'M UNBALANCED.

305
00:11:04,736 --> 00:11:06,504
YOU
UNDERSTAND?

306
00:11:06,504 --> 00:11:09,607
AND YOU'RE WEARING A CROWN ON
YOUR HEAD, YOU LOOK RIDICULOUS.

307
00:11:09,607 --> 00:11:11,876
THEY AIN'T EVEN
REAL DIAMONDS.

308
00:11:11,876 --> 00:11:14,479
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,
BABY.

309
00:11:14,479 --> 00:11:17,248
RECOGNIZE,
AND DON'T FORGET.

310
00:11:17,248 --> 00:11:19,751
AND YOU WEAR THAT CROWN,
MISS DIVA, YOU WEAR IT,

311
00:11:19,751 --> 00:11:23,221
'CAUSE BELIEVE ME, YOU WILL SEE
WHO IS THE DIVA.

312
00:11:24,622 --> 00:11:26,791
THE HOT TEMPERS IN THE HOUSE
COOLED DOWN

313
00:11:26,791 --> 00:11:28,726
AT THE NEXT DAY'S
PHOTO SHOOT.

314
00:11:28,726 --> 00:11:33,765
TODAY'S SHOOT IS ON THIS AMAZING
SET MADE OF ICE.

315
00:11:33,765 --> 00:11:36,501
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT,
HOLD ON.

316
00:11:36,501 --> 00:11:38,236
OH, THAT IS SO MEAN.

317
00:11:38,236 --> 00:11:39,771
I LIVED IN AFRICA
FOR 12 YEARS,

318
00:11:39,771 --> 00:11:41,672
IT DOESN'T GO
BELOW 80 DEGREES.

319
00:11:41,672 --> 00:11:44,409
AND I LIVE IN TEXAS NOW,
AND I'VE NEVER SEEN SNOW, SO.

320
00:11:44,409 --> 00:11:46,277
WELL, NOW YOU'RE GONNA
GET YOUR LESSON

321
00:11:46,277 --> 00:11:48,179
AND YOU HAVE NO HAIR
TO KEEP YOU WARM

322
00:11:48,179 --> 00:11:49,914
AND I DON'T HAVE A HAT
FOR YOU, EITHER.

323
00:11:49,914 --> 00:11:51,315
SO YOUR CHALLENGE IS NOW--

324
00:11:51,315 --> 00:11:52,483
YOU CAN GIVE ME--

325
00:11:52,483 --> 00:11:55,420
OH, HELL NO,
I'M NOT GIVING YOU MY HAT.

326
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:57,688
THE CHALLENGE WAS CHILLING
FOR THE GIRLS.

327
00:11:57,688 --> 00:12:00,691
JUST LIKE THAT.

328
00:12:00,691 --> 00:12:03,594
I THINK MOST PEOPLE WOULD BE
EXCITED TO WEAR A DIAMOND THONG,

329
00:12:03,594 --> 00:12:05,329
BUT IT'S A COMPLETELY
DIFFERENT STORY

330
00:12:05,329 --> 00:12:07,665
WHEN YOU HAVE TO SIT DOWN
FOR AN EXTENDED PERIOD OF TIME

331
00:12:07,665 --> 00:12:09,634
ON A BENCH
MADE OF ICE.

332
00:12:09,634 --> 00:12:11,803
MY FEAR WAS THAT MY BUTT WAS
GONNA STICK TO IT.

333
00:12:11,803 --> 00:12:12,837
USUALLY,
WHEN YOU'RE TAKING PICTURES,

334
00:12:12,837 --> 00:12:15,706
IF IT FEELS REALLY AWKWARD,
IT LOOKS GREAT

335
00:12:15,706 --> 00:12:17,875
AND THIS WAS ONE
OF THOSE TIMES

336
00:12:17,875 --> 00:12:19,911
WHERE PRETTY MUCH EVERYTHING
FELT AWKWARD.

337
00:12:19,911 --> 00:12:21,179
GOOD, CHIN DOWN.

338
00:12:21,179 --> 00:12:22,280
LITTLE MORE.

339
00:12:22,280 --> 00:12:23,548
WITH HER MIND
ON OTHER THINGS,

340
00:12:23,548 --> 00:12:25,416
WENDY COULDN'T FOCUS
ON HER POSES.

341
00:12:25,416 --> 00:12:27,185
OKAY, WENDY,
LET ME SHOW YOU SOMETHING.

342
00:12:27,185 --> 00:12:28,586
DOES THAT
LOOK PRETTY?

343
00:12:28,586 --> 00:12:31,756
I FEEL LIKE WENDY'S STATE
OF MIND READS ON HER FACE.

344
00:12:31,756 --> 00:12:32,890
A LITTLE
LESS SEVERE.

345
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:34,225
GOOD, BEAUTIFUL.

346
00:12:34,225 --> 00:12:35,927
STILL THROWN OFF
BY HER NEW LOOK,

347
00:12:35,927 --> 00:12:39,230
JADE LET THE CHILLY ATMOSPHERE
CREEP UP INTO HER FACE.

348
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:41,732
IT'S NOT A SQUINT,
IT'S A SMILE.

349
00:12:41,732 --> 00:12:43,201
THAT'S A SMILE?

350
00:12:43,201 --> 00:12:44,569
MY EYES
ARE JUST DIFFERENT.

351
00:12:46,370 --> 00:12:49,474
AT JUDGING, THE PANEL WAS NOT
IMPRESSED WITH JADE'S PHOTO.

352
00:12:49,474 --> 00:12:50,975
NOW, WHY PROFILE?

353
00:12:50,975 --> 00:12:53,411
I JUST DON'T THINK
YOU CAN DO A COVER SHOT

354
00:12:53,411 --> 00:12:55,246
AND NOT LOOK
AT THE CAMERA.

355
00:12:55,246 --> 00:12:57,248
I MEAN,
IT JUST DOESN'T WORK.

356
00:12:57,248 --> 00:12:58,683
BUT IT WAS THE VACANCY IN
WENDY'S EYES

357
00:12:58,683 --> 00:13:00,318
THAT WORRIED
THE PANEL.

358
00:13:00,318 --> 00:13:01,919
THE JUDGES SEE A MODEL
IN PERSON.

359
00:13:01,919 --> 00:13:05,623
THEY HAVEN'T SEEN THAT POTENTIAL
PUT INTO A PHOTO.

360
00:13:07,725 --> 00:13:10,928
SO JADE SURVIVED AND
WENDY WAS ELIMINATED.

361
00:13:10,928 --> 00:13:14,699
AND WENDY, YOU HAVE HAD
A LONG, LONG JOURNEY

362
00:13:14,699 --> 00:13:18,569
AND YOU HAVE GONE
THROUGH HELL AND BACK,

363
00:13:18,569 --> 00:13:20,238
BUT YOU'RE HERE.

364
00:13:20,238 --> 00:13:24,342
AND WHAT YOU REPRESENT TO ME
IS SOMEBODY THAT'S STRONG,

365
00:13:24,342 --> 00:13:28,613
SOMEBODY THAT PERSEVERES
IN THE FACE OF ADVERSITY.

366
00:13:28,613 --> 00:13:30,815
SO WHEN YOU GO
TO BED AT NIGHT,

367
00:13:30,815 --> 00:13:32,617
I DON'T WANT YOU
TO FEEL LIKE A LOSER,

368
00:13:32,617 --> 00:13:34,552
BECAUSE
IN MY BOOK,

369
00:13:34,552 --> 00:13:35,786
YOU'RE A WINNER.

370
00:13:35,786 --> 00:13:36,954
AND I MEAN
THAT.

371
00:13:36,954 --> 00:13:38,456
GIVE ME
A HUG.

372
00:13:43,461 --> 00:13:44,896
YOU CAN
STILL MODEL.

373
00:13:44,896 --> 00:13:46,531
YOU'RE NOT GONNA BE
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL,

374
00:13:46,531 --> 00:13:47,965
BUT YOU CAN
STILL MODEL.

375
00:13:47,965 --> 00:13:49,600
THANK YOU...

376
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:52,236
FOR BRINGING ME
THIS FAR.

377
00:13:52,236 --> 00:13:53,604
THANK YOU.

378
00:14:00,411 --> 00:14:02,280
AFTER A FEW WEEKS
IN THE COMPETITION,

379
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:04,749
THE GIRLS STARTED GETTING
COMFORTABLE AND OPENING UP.

380
00:14:04,749 --> 00:14:05,850
DO YOU KNOW I LOOKED EXACTLY
LIKE MISS PIGGY

381
00:14:05,850 --> 00:14:06,951
WHEN I WAS LITTLE?

382
00:14:06,951 --> 00:14:08,386
I WAS SO FAT.

383
00:14:08,386 --> 00:14:10,855
LIKE, ABNORMALLY FAT
WHEN I CAME OUT.

384
00:14:10,855 --> 00:14:12,790
IF I WORE CORDUROY,

385
00:14:12,790 --> 00:14:16,494
I WOULD, LIKE, START FIRES
WITH MY THIGHS.

386
00:14:16,494 --> 00:14:18,963
AND SOME OF THE GIRLS
GOT TOO COMFORTABLE.

387
00:14:18,963 --> 00:14:20,965
HOW MANY SHOES DO YOU HAVE,
LIKE, TOTAL?

388
00:14:20,965 --> 00:14:22,333
I DON'T EVEN--

389
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:23,734
MY DAD, HAS,
LIKE SHELVES BUILT.

390
00:14:23,734 --> 00:14:25,469
I LOVE HANGING OUT
WITH DANIELLE,

391
00:14:25,469 --> 00:14:27,204
SHE'S REALLY COOL,
I LIKE HER HUMOR.

392
00:14:27,204 --> 00:14:28,906
(crunching)
OW, GINA!

393
00:14:28,906 --> 00:14:31,943
I CAN'T HELP IT, LIKE,
THE MORE YOU JUST,

394
00:14:31,943 --> 00:14:34,245
LIKE, WE'RE TALKING,
I JUST--

395
00:14:34,245 --> 00:14:35,780
I DON'T KNOW WHAT IS WRONG
WITH GINA,

396
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,782
BUT DANG, I'M SCARED,
FOR REAL.

397
00:14:37,782 --> 00:14:39,684
HAVE YOU DONE THAT
ALL YOUR LIFE?

398
00:14:39,684 --> 00:14:41,218
UM, LIKE,
THE PAST YEAR.

399
00:14:41,218 --> 00:14:42,887
THIS GIRL RIGHT HERE,

400
00:14:42,887 --> 00:14:43,888
SHE'S OFF
THE WALL.

401
00:14:43,888 --> 00:14:45,957
YEAH, SHE BITES,
INSTEAD OF KISSES.

402
00:14:45,957 --> 00:14:47,258
SHE BITES.

403
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:51,562
I JUST WANNA,
LIKE, BITE YOU.

404
00:14:51,562 --> 00:14:52,597
I DID THAT
WITH HER,

405
00:14:52,597 --> 00:14:53,698
I DID IT
WITH A FEW OTHERS.

406
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:57,935
WELL, I DON'T, LIKE, TASTE THEM,
I JUST GO, LIKE--

407
00:14:57,935 --> 00:15:00,571
I'M LIKE,
"WHAT PAGE ARE YOU ON, HONEY?"

408
00:15:00,571 --> 00:15:01,772
'CAUSE WE'RE ON,
LIKE, 14,

409
00:15:01,772 --> 00:15:02,940
YOU'RE ON, LIKE,
40 MILLION.

410
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,742
WE KNOW WHAT YOU DO
WITH YOUR BOYFRIEND.

411
00:15:04,742 --> 00:15:06,243
GOD, YOU GOT
A PROBLEM.

412
00:15:06,243 --> 00:15:07,612
THAT'S NOT NORMAL.

413
00:15:07,612 --> 00:15:10,214
SOMETIMES I'M NOT EVEN AWARE
THAT I'M DOING IT.

414
00:15:10,214 --> 00:15:11,282
RIGHT THERE, STOP.

415
00:15:11,282 --> 00:15:12,316
OKAY, I'M DONE.

416
00:15:13,951 --> 00:15:16,887
LATER THAT DAY, I HAD A CRYPTIC
MESSAGE FOR THE GIRLS.

417
00:15:16,887 --> 00:15:18,956
I DON'T THINK
I CAN PRONOUNCE THIS.

418
00:15:18,956 --> 00:15:21,726
"GROMPHADORINA
PORTENTOSA."

419
00:15:21,726 --> 00:15:23,728
WHAT IN THE WORLD
IS THAT?

420
00:15:23,728 --> 00:15:25,763
GROMPHADORINA...

421
00:15:25,763 --> 00:15:29,400
GRUMPA...
SKRILLIUMPTIOUS!

422
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:31,669
L.A. DESIGNER JARED GOLD
WAS KIND ENOUGH

423
00:15:31,669 --> 00:15:34,672
TO HELP THE GIRLS FIGURE OUT
JUST WHAT MY CLUE MEANT.

424
00:15:34,672 --> 00:15:37,341
THESE ARE GIANT MADAGASCAR
HISSING COCKROACHES.

425
00:15:37,341 --> 00:15:38,309
(gasping)

426
00:15:41,212 --> 00:15:43,447
WE HAVE ACTUALLY USED THESE
ROACHES IN RUNWAY SHOWS BEFORE.

427
00:15:43,447 --> 00:15:45,616
OH, DON'T
DO THIS.

428
00:15:45,616 --> 00:15:47,485
EVERYBODY'S GOING TO HAVE
TO WEAR ONE OF THESE.

429
00:15:47,485 --> 00:15:48,853
(gasping)

430
00:15:48,853 --> 00:15:50,655
I SEE THESE LITTLE THINGS,
LIKE, MOVING

431
00:15:50,655 --> 00:15:52,823
AND I SEE THE LEGS MOVING
AND I'M LIKE, OH!

432
00:15:52,823 --> 00:15:54,258
THEY'RE ABOUT
150 BUCKS EACH.

433
00:15:54,258 --> 00:15:55,459
THE ROACHES?

434
00:15:55,459 --> 00:15:56,594
- UH-HUH.
- WHAT?

435
00:15:56,594 --> 00:15:58,496
FOR $150, YOU COULD HAVE
YOUR OWN LITTLE PET

436
00:15:58,496 --> 00:15:59,563
CRAWLING ON YOU
AT ALL TIMES.

437
00:15:59,563 --> 00:16:00,765
IT'S A GREAT DEAL.

438
00:16:00,765 --> 00:16:02,833
I'M SO PROUD,
NO ONE'S CRYING YET.

439
00:16:04,468 --> 00:16:06,537
GO!

440
00:16:06,537 --> 00:16:09,774
I WOULD NOT WEAR THIS
IN MY CASKET AT MY FUNERAL,

441
00:16:09,774 --> 00:16:11,208
BUT I WALKED IT,

442
00:16:11,208 --> 00:16:12,410
'CAUSE THAT'S WHAT YOU GOTTA DO
WHEN YOU A MODEL.

443
00:16:12,410 --> 00:16:14,211
YOU CAN'T COMPLAIN.

444
00:16:14,211 --> 00:16:15,946
THE ROACH I HAD ON ME
HAD EATEN HIS LEG OFF,

445
00:16:15,946 --> 00:16:17,748
WHICH IS WHY HE DIDN'T
MOVE A LOT

446
00:16:17,748 --> 00:16:20,418
AND I ALMOST FELT BAD
FOR THE ROACH.

447
00:16:20,418 --> 00:16:21,919
OKAY, GO.

448
00:16:21,919 --> 00:16:22,920
HE'S PISSED.

449
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:25,589
(laughing)
DID YOU SEE THAT?

450
00:16:25,589 --> 00:16:27,692
SHE TOOK IT
IN HER HAND!

451
00:16:27,692 --> 00:16:32,329
JADE'S BOLDNESS
BLEW JARED GOLD AWAY.

452
00:16:32,329 --> 00:16:33,931
OH, SHE KISSED IT!

453
00:16:33,931 --> 00:16:37,234
DUDE, THEY LOVED IT
AND I WAS LIKE, HELL YES.

454
00:16:37,234 --> 00:16:39,270
JADE,
YOU'RE AWESOME.

455
00:16:39,270 --> 00:16:40,638
BUT SOME
TRIUMPHANT TEASING--

456
