686
00:25:34,438 --> 00:25:36,540
JAY SEEMS A LITTLE
OBSESSIVE-COMPULSIVE

687
00:25:36,540 --> 00:25:39,376
AS FAR AS, YOU KNOW,
CLEANLINESS GOES.

688
00:25:39,376 --> 00:25:41,478
ALL RIGHT,
I'M GONNA GO.

689
00:25:41,478 --> 00:25:42,779
OH, YOU'RE NOT GONNA HAVE
BREAKFAST WITH US NOW?

690
00:25:42,779 --> 00:25:44,314
OH, NO, I'M GOING
THROUGH A DRIVE-THRU.

691
00:25:46,583 --> 00:25:48,252
YOU DIDN'T DO
THE DISHES YET.

692
00:25:48,252 --> 00:25:50,520
WE HAVE THIS BAD STENCH
IN THE KITCHEN

693
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:52,489
AND IT MAKES ME THROW UP
A LITTLE BIT IN MY MOUTH.

694
00:25:52,489 --> 00:25:53,557
LOOK AT THAT.

695
00:25:53,557 --> 00:25:54,558
LET'S SEE IT.

696
00:25:54,558 --> 00:25:55,759
THAT IS
DISCOLORED.

697
00:25:55,759 --> 00:25:58,462
EW, IT SMELLS LIKE DEAD FLESH,
LIKE ROADKILL!

698
00:25:58,462 --> 00:26:01,198
I'LL GIVE YOU $100
TO EAT THIS.

699
00:26:01,198 --> 00:26:01,798
GET OUT OF HERE!

700
00:26:01,798 --> 00:26:02,633
$100?

701
00:26:02,633 --> 00:26:05,669
$100?-- I'LL HAVE E. COLI
AND BE DEAD AT 6:00 A.M.

702
00:26:05,669 --> 00:26:07,404
BUT YOU GONNA
HAVE $100.

703
00:26:07,404 --> 00:26:09,573
FURONDA,
YOU WANT SOME MONEY?

704
00:26:09,573 --> 00:26:11,675
GO GET
THE HUNDRED DOLLARS.

705
00:26:11,675 --> 00:26:13,410
THESE GIRLS
ARE FILTHY.

706
00:26:13,410 --> 00:26:16,480
THEY EAT AND LEAVE PLATES OUT
WITH FOOD STILL ON 'EM.

707
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:18,415
LOOK AT THIS--
BAM!

708
00:26:18,415 --> 00:26:19,516
BAM, BAM.

709
00:26:19,516 --> 00:26:20,684
BAM, BAM.

710
00:26:20,684 --> 00:26:21,918
BAM!

711
00:26:21,918 --> 00:26:23,954
WHAT ELSE
CAN WE THROW AWAY?

712
00:26:23,954 --> 00:26:25,756
OH, WE'RE THROWING
THAT AWAY.

713
00:26:25,756 --> 00:26:26,623
YOU SO STUPID.

714
00:26:27,190 --> 00:26:29,226
WHILE SOME GIRLS FOCUSED ON
CLEANING UP,

715
00:26:29,226 --> 00:26:31,662
MOLLIE SUE WORRIED ABOUT HER
PLACE IN THE COMPETITION.

716
00:26:35,799 --> 00:26:37,634
LIKE, EVEN LOOKING
AROUND, LIKE,

717
00:26:37,634 --> 00:26:38,902
THERE'S LESS
GIRLS HERE.

718
00:26:38,902 --> 00:26:40,837
AND PEOPLE JUST TURN,
YOU KNOW, LIKE,

719
00:26:40,837 --> 00:26:41,905
THE PEOPLE
YOU THINK--

720
00:26:41,905 --> 00:26:43,206
AND NOW YOU REALLY
START FEELING IT,

721
00:26:43,206 --> 00:26:44,374
YOU START SEEING
YOUR COMPETITION.

722
00:26:44,374 --> 00:26:44,775
YEAH.

723
00:26:44,775 --> 00:26:46,843
RIGHT NOW,
THINGS ARE JUST, LIKE,

724
00:26:46,843 --> 00:26:47,944
THE MOST STRESSFUL
THEY'VE BEEN.

725
00:26:47,944 --> 00:26:49,813
I GUESS IT'S PROBABLY
GONNA GET WORSE.

726
00:26:49,813 --> 00:26:51,481
IT'S KIND OF
TAKEN A TOLL.

727
00:26:52,549 --> 00:26:54,885
A TOP MODEL HAS
TO THINK ON HER FEET

728
00:26:54,885 --> 00:26:57,754
AS THE GIRLS SOON LEARNED
IN A COMMERCIAL FOR COVERGIRL.

729
00:26:57,754 --> 00:26:59,323
WHAT WE'RE GONNA DO
IS GIVE YOU GIRLS

730
00:26:59,323 --> 00:27:02,192
A COUPLE OF LINES
THAT YOU HAVE TO LAND.

731
00:27:02,192 --> 00:27:03,760
NOW, THE REST OF THE SPOT
IS ALL UP TO YOU

732
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:05,228
'CAUSE IT'S ABOUT
IMPROVISATION.

733
00:27:05,228 --> 00:27:08,465
WE HAD 30 SECONDS TO, LIKE,
WALK UP THE STAIRS,

734
00:27:08,465 --> 00:27:10,901
AROUND, BY THE POOL AND THEN
STOP AND LAND OUR LINES.

735
00:27:13,203 --> 00:27:14,971
PARTIES ARE
SO UNPREDICTABLE.

736
00:27:14,971 --> 00:27:16,807
BUT YOUR MAKEUP
DOESN'T HAVE TO BE.

737
00:27:16,807 --> 00:27:17,974
THAT'S
A GOOD LINE.

738
00:27:17,974 --> 00:27:19,943
WHEN I WEAR COVERGIRL ,
I KNOW I LOOK GOOD.

739
00:27:19,943 --> 00:27:21,511
HEY, EVERYONE.

740
00:27:21,511 --> 00:27:22,946
DERMATOLOGIST-TESTED.

741
00:27:22,946 --> 00:27:24,881
SHEER,
LIGHTWEIGHT COVERAGE.

742
00:27:24,881 --> 00:27:27,417
EASY, BREEZY,
BEAUTIFUL.

743
00:27:27,417 --> 00:27:29,286
COVERGIRL.

744
00:27:29,286 --> 00:27:30,420
AND CUT.

745
00:27:30,420 --> 00:27:31,888
PERSONALLY,
I KNOW I DID GOOD TODAY.

746
00:27:31,888 --> 00:27:33,323
SEVERAL GIRLS
STRUGGLED.

747
00:27:34,591 --> 00:27:36,626
SHEER.

748
00:27:36,626 --> 00:27:38,729
IT'S LONG-LASTING.

749
00:27:38,729 --> 00:27:40,530
DERMATOLOGIST-TESTED.

750
00:27:40,530 --> 00:27:44,267
THERE WAS NOTHING ENGAGING
ABOUT THAT DELIVERY.

751
00:27:44,267 --> 00:27:45,869
WONDERFUL,
FABULOUS.

752
00:27:45,869 --> 00:27:48,205
SHE'S
A DRAG QUEEN.

753
00:27:48,205 --> 00:27:50,474
THIS IS...

754
00:27:50,474 --> 00:27:51,575
(beep)

755
00:27:51,575 --> 00:27:54,678
LIGHTWEIGHT MAKEUP.

756
00:27:54,678 --> 00:27:56,580
(bleep)
CUT!

757
00:27:56,580 --> 00:27:58,315
COVER GIRLS
DON'T SAY THAT.

758
00:27:58,315 --> 00:27:59,716
BUT WHEN BROOKE FUMBLED...

759
00:27:59,716 --> 00:28:02,786
SHEER LIGHT COVERAGE
MAKEUP.

760
00:28:02,786 --> 00:28:04,354
(sighing)

761
00:28:04,354 --> 00:28:05,355
CUT!

762
00:28:05,355 --> 00:28:06,189
SHE LOST
HER COMPOSURE.

763
00:28:07,891 --> 00:28:09,192
I DON'T WANNA TALK
ABOUT IT.

764
00:28:14,264 --> 00:28:16,666
AT JUDGING,
JADE WAS FULL OF EXCUSES.

765
00:28:16,666 --> 00:28:18,235
ALL RIGHTY, JADE,
SO YOU HAD A COMMERCIAL.

766
00:28:18,235 --> 00:28:19,636
AND HERE'S
YOUR BEST TAKE.

767
00:28:19,636 --> 00:28:21,938
THIS IS...

768
00:28:21,938 --> 00:28:22,873
OKAY.

769
00:28:23,940 --> 00:28:25,609
YOU GUYS USED
MY WORST ONE.

770
00:28:25,609 --> 00:28:27,411
I CAN'T IMAGINE,
THOUGH,

771
00:28:27,411 --> 00:28:29,713
HOW DIFFERENT YOU WOULD
HAVE DONE ANOTHER ONE

772
00:28:29,713 --> 00:28:31,448
BECAUSE YOU'D HAVE
TO BE NIGHT AND DAY.

773
00:28:31,448 --> 00:28:33,617
I HAVE WORKED FOR VICTORIA'S
SECRET FOR TEN YEARS

774
00:28:33,617 --> 00:28:35,952
AND I'M LIKE, "WHY THE HELL DID
THEY CHOOSE THAT SHOT?"

775
00:28:35,952 --> 00:28:38,288
BUT FOR SOME REASON,
IT WORKS FOR THEM.

776
00:28:38,288 --> 00:28:40,690
YOU'LL NEVER BE 100 PERCENT
HAPPY AS A MODEL.

777
00:28:40,690 --> 00:28:45,495
BUT IT WAS MOLLIE SUE
WHO STOOD OUT IN THE WRONG WAY.

778
00:28:45,495 --> 00:28:49,399
FOR A LATE NIGHT, I WANT
SOMETHING LIGHT AND HASSLE-FREE.

779
00:28:49,399 --> 00:28:50,734
SHEER.

780
00:28:50,734 --> 00:28:52,903
LONG-LASTING.

781
00:28:52,903 --> 00:28:54,771
DERMATOLOGIST-TESTED.

782
00:28:54,771 --> 00:28:56,440
IT WASN'T
A MODEL'S PERFORMANCE.

783
00:28:56,440 --> 00:28:58,475
IT WAS ALMOST LIKE
YOU WERE SELLING MACE.

784
00:28:58,475 --> 00:28:59,910
"YOU WANNA
KEEP 'EM AWAY?"

785
00:28:59,910 --> 00:29:01,445
"YOU WANT ME TO--"
YOU KNOW?

786
00:29:01,445 --> 00:29:05,949
AND HER SHORTCOMINGS ON CAMERA
GOT HER SENT HOME.

787
00:29:05,949 --> 00:29:08,351
I'M SO CONFUSED
RIGHT NOW.

788
00:29:08,351 --> 00:29:12,489
FOR JADE TO STAY OVER ME,
IT WAS JUST CRAZY.

789
00:29:12,489 --> 00:29:16,259
NIGEL, MISS J, MR. JAY,
TWIGGY, EVERYONE,

790
00:29:16,259 --> 00:29:18,295
YOU JUST KICKED
YOUR WINNER OFF FIFTH, SO.

791
00:29:22,699 --> 00:29:24,868
THE COMPETITION FOR "AMERICA'S
NEXT TOP MODEL" CAN BE TOUGH,

792
00:29:24,868 --> 00:29:26,536
BUT FOR NNENNA,

793
00:29:26,536 --> 00:29:29,439
A NEEDY BOYFRIEND BACK HOME
MADE THINGS EVEN HARDER.

794
00:29:29,439 --> 00:29:30,941
You can't even--

795
00:29:30,941 --> 00:29:32,776
you can't give me all this truth
of your intentions.

796
00:29:32,776 --> 00:29:34,277
JOHN, JOHN.

797
00:29:34,277 --> 00:29:35,612
You did.

798
00:29:35,612 --> 00:29:37,581
SHE'S LIKE, "JOHN, NO, DON'T
TALK MY PERSONAL BUSINESS.

799
00:29:37,581 --> 00:29:39,382
"JOHN, JOHN!

800
00:29:39,382 --> 00:29:42,619
"I'M NOT GONNA TALK
TO YOU IF-- JOHN!"

801
00:29:42,619 --> 00:29:44,788
YOU'RE NOT LISTENING.

802
00:29:44,788 --> 00:29:45,789
NO, YOU'RE NOT.

803
00:29:45,789 --> 00:29:47,290
NO,
YOU'RE NOT.

804
00:29:47,290 --> 00:29:48,525
WHAT IF I BROKE UP
WITH YOU RIGHT NOW?

805
00:29:55,699 --> 00:29:57,501
NNENNA BEEN ON THE PHONE
FOR AN HOUR.

806
00:29:57,501 --> 00:29:59,603
SHE ON THE PHONE LIKE SHE IN HER
APARTMENT OR SOMETHING.

807
00:29:59,603 --> 00:30:02,539
NNENNA IS ON THE PHONE WITH HER
BOYFRIEND, LIKE, WAY TOO LONG.

808
00:30:02,539 --> 00:30:03,974
I DO UNDERSTAND,
LIKE,

809
00:30:03,974 --> 00:30:06,409
YOU'RE HAVING DIFFICULTIES WITH
YOUR BOYFRIEND AND EVERYTHING,

810
00:30:06,409 --> 00:30:08,712
BUT THERE IS EIGHT PEOPLE
IN THE HOUSE.

811
00:30:08,712 --> 00:30:10,413
SHE MONOPOLIZES
THE PHONE

812
00:30:10,413 --> 00:30:11,815
AND WHEN I TRY
TO TALK TO HER

813
00:30:11,815 --> 00:30:13,950
AND BE CONSIDERATE AND DECENT
TO HER, WHAT DOES SHE DO?

814
00:30:13,950 --> 00:30:15,585
SHE HAS
TO LAUGH AT ME.

815
00:30:15,585 --> 00:30:18,688
EVERYBODY DOES HAVE A BREAKING
POINT TO HOW MUCH THEY CAN TAKE.

816
00:30:18,688 --> 00:30:20,423
I JUST GOT
TO MY BREAKING POINT.

817
00:30:20,423 --> 00:30:22,192
I'M NOT REALLY
A MEAN PERSON

818
00:30:22,192 --> 00:30:24,761
BUT DEFINITELY I THINK
WHEN I GET IRRITATED

819
00:30:24,761 --> 00:30:27,898
OR ANGRY OR FRUSTRATED,
I BECOME WICKED.

820
00:30:27,898 --> 00:30:29,766
YOU CRY A LOT,
SO YOU KNOW,

821
00:30:29,766 --> 00:30:31,968
BEING EMOTIONAL RIGHT NOW
ISN'T GONNA BOTHER ME.

822
00:30:34,471 --> 00:30:35,539
WHAT HAPPENED?

823
00:30:35,539 --> 00:30:36,840
THERE IS EIGHT PEOPLE
IN THE HOUSE.

824
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:38,308
SHE IS NOT
THE ONLY ONE,

825
00:30:38,308 --> 00:30:39,609
THIS IS NOT HER HOUSE,
THIS IS NOT HER PHONE.

826
00:30:39,609 --> 00:30:40,677
SHE LAUGHS
AT ME.

827
00:30:40,677 --> 00:30:41,344
YOU KNOW WHAT?

828
00:30:41,344 --> 00:30:43,380
HAVE TACT, HAVE CONSIDERATION
OF OTHER PEOPLE.

829
00:30:43,380 --> 00:30:44,915
I CAN ONLY TAKE
SO MUCH.

830
00:30:44,915 --> 00:30:46,816
THE GIRLS KNOW THAT WALKING
A STRAIGHT LINE DOWN THE RUNWAY

831
00:30:46,816 --> 00:30:48,852
IS NOT AS EASY
AS IT SEEMS,

832
00:30:48,852 --> 00:30:51,788
BUT THEY HADN'T SEEN ANYTHING
UNTIL THEY SAW THE SWIRL.

833
00:30:51,788 --> 00:30:52,856
A SWIRL!

834
00:30:52,856 --> 00:30:53,924
I'M RICHARD HARRIS.

835
00:30:53,924 --> 00:30:55,425
AND I'M RON HARRIS.

836
00:30:55,425 --> 00:30:57,460
AND WE'RE GONNA TEACH YOU
A SWIRL.

837
00:30:57,460 --> 00:30:59,262
IT'S A MOVEMENT.

838
00:30:59,262 --> 00:31:02,365
THE SKIRT IS MOVING, THE GOWN IS
MOVING, THE HAIR IS MOVING,

839
00:31:02,365 --> 00:31:05,869
BUT HER PERSONALITY AND AURA
IS THE SAME.

840
00:31:05,869 --> 00:31:09,906
♪♪♪

841
00:31:09,906 --> 00:31:11,675
RON AND RICH,
THE TWINS,

842
00:31:11,675 --> 00:31:13,843
THEY TEACH US
HOW TO SWIRL

843
00:31:13,843 --> 00:31:15,612
AND THEY'RE SO FUNNY
AND SO CUTE.

844
00:31:15,612 --> 00:31:17,447
OKAY.

845
00:31:17,447 --> 00:31:18,648
WORK THE MOVEMENT,
WORK THE BODY.

846
00:31:18,648 --> 00:31:19,649
MAKE ME
FEEL IT.

847
00:31:19,649 --> 00:31:20,951
SELF-CONFIDENT.

848
00:31:20,951 --> 00:31:22,552
THAT'S WHAT A MODEL
IS ALL ABOUT.

849
00:31:22,552 --> 00:31:25,355
I CAN SELL IT, I CAN MOVE IT,
I CAN DO IT.

850
00:31:25,355 --> 00:31:26,723
SWIRL, SWIRL, SWIRL.

851
00:31:27,757 --> 00:31:29,593
RON AND RICHARD
WERE ECCENTRIC.

852
00:31:29,593 --> 00:31:30,794
THAT'S THE BEST WAY
TO DESCRIBE THEM.

853
00:31:30,794 --> 00:31:31,828
THEY WERE
ECCENTRIC.

854
00:31:31,828 --> 00:31:32,662
THEIR AURA
WAS GREAT.

855
00:31:32,662 --> 00:31:34,564
♪♪♪

856
00:31:35,865 --> 00:31:37,767
SARA DID NOT PERFECT
THE TECHNIQUE

857
00:31:37,767 --> 00:31:40,337
BY THE END
OF THE TEACH.

858
00:31:40,337 --> 00:31:43,340
SARA WASN'T THE ONLY ONE WHO
HAD TROUBLE WITH THEIR WALK.

859
00:31:43,340 --> 00:31:45,342
I CAME BACK HOME
AND PRACTICED MY RUNWAY WALK.

860
00:31:45,342 --> 00:31:47,277
SWIRL.

861
00:31:47,277 --> 00:31:49,879
I THINK I'M LEARNING HOW TO NOT
WALK WITH MY BUTT OUT.

862
00:31:49,879 --> 00:31:51,448
I DIDN'T KNOW I WALKED
WITH MY BUTT OUT.

863
00:31:51,448 --> 00:31:52,816
LIKE, I DON'T FEEL LIKE
I'M STICKING MY BUTT OUT,

864
00:31:52,816 --> 00:31:53,850
BUT I GUESS
IT'S OUT.

865
00:31:53,850 --> 00:31:55,352
I CAN'T WALK
LIKE THAT

866
00:31:55,352 --> 00:31:56,620
WITHOUT FEELING LIKE
I'M GONNA FALL, YOU KNOW?

867
00:31:56,620 --> 00:31:58,622
MY WALK IS
JUST HORRIBLE.

868
00:31:58,622 --> 00:31:59,889
I ALWAYS THOUGHT
I DON'T HAVE AN ASS,

869
00:31:59,889 --> 00:32:01,725
LIKE, HOW CAN I BE WALKING
WITH MY BUTT OUT?

870
00:32:01,725 --> 00:32:02,759
(woman on phone)
You do!

871
00:32:02,759 --> 00:32:03,660
I DIDN'T
KNOW THIS.

872
00:32:03,660 --> 00:32:04,961
LIKE, WHY DOESN'T ANYONE
TELL ME THIS?

873
00:32:05,462 --> 00:32:06,563
THE PHOTO SHOOT
THAT WEEK

874
00:32:06,563 --> 00:32:08,832
WAS ALL ABOUT UNDERSTANDING
BODY MOVEMENT,

875
00:32:08,832 --> 00:32:09,866
AS THE GIRLS
WERE JOINED

876
00:32:09,866 --> 00:32:12,869
BY THE PIONEERS OF A DANCE
STYLE KNOWN AS "KRUMPING".

877
00:32:12,869 --> 00:32:14,571
(chanting)
♪ HEY LADIES
HEY LADIES ♪

878
00:32:14,571 --> 00:32:16,206
♪ HEY LADIES ♪

879
00:32:16,206 --> 00:32:19,342
KRUMPING IS, LIKE, THIS REAL
INTENSE WAY OF DANCING.

880
00:32:19,342 --> 00:32:21,211
A LOT
OF BODY MOVEMENT.

881
00:32:27,317 --> 00:32:28,385
THERE YOU GO!

882
00:32:28,385 --> 00:32:29,619
SOME GIRLS
ROCKED IT OUT.

883
00:32:29,619 --> 00:32:33,957
WOO!

884
00:32:33,957 --> 00:32:36,426
AND SOME GIRLS JUST COULDN'T
LET IT ALL HANG OUT.

885
00:32:38,628 --> 00:32:39,796
IS THAT HOW YOU DANCE
FOR THE MEN?

886
00:32:39,796 --> 00:32:41,398
I WANT YOU TO BE
IN THE CLUB.

887
00:32:41,398 --> 00:32:42,732
I NEED
TO FEEL IT MORE.

888
00:32:45,201 --> 00:32:46,603
SO AT THE END
OF THE DAY,

889
00:32:46,603 --> 00:32:48,371
THE GIRLS BLEW OFF SOME STEAM
WITH A KRUMP-OFF.

890
00:32:48,371 --> 00:32:51,408
WE GOT TO DO
A LITTLE BATTLE

891
00:32:51,408 --> 00:32:53,510
WHERE YOU WALK UP
TO THE PERSON YOU'RE BATTLING

892
00:32:53,510 --> 00:32:54,778
AND YOU JUST SHOW 'EM
YOUR MOVES

893
00:32:54,778 --> 00:32:55,812
AND THEN THEY HAVE
TO DO THE SAME.

894
00:32:55,812 --> 00:32:56,813
WOO!

895
00:32:56,813 --> 00:32:57,814
WOO!

896
00:32:57,814 --> 00:32:58,882
WOO!

897
00:32:58,882 --> 00:33:00,316
WOO!

898
00:33:00,316 --> 00:33:01,785
OH!

899
00:33:01,785 --> 00:33:03,586
OH!

900
00:33:06,489 --> 00:33:07,757
GO JOANIE!

901
00:33:07,757 --> 00:33:09,359
GO JOANIE!

902
00:33:09,359 --> 00:33:12,495
I PUT MY HOOD OVER MY HEAD
AND I GOT ALL DOWN AND DIRTY.

903
00:33:12,495 --> 00:33:13,863
WHAT.

904
00:33:13,863 --> 00:33:16,666
OH, OH, OH, OH, OH!

905
00:33:16,666 --> 00:33:17,634
OH!

906
00:33:17,634 --> 00:33:18,868
OH!

907
00:33:18,868 --> 00:33:20,403
I NOTICED
WHEN I WALKED UP TO HER,

908
00:33:20,403 --> 00:33:22,706
LIKE, I CAN JUST SEE FEAR
IN HER EYES.

909
00:33:25,341 --> 00:33:26,910
THAT'S KRUMP DANCING
RIGHT THERE.

910
00:33:26,910 --> 00:33:27,977
HO!

911
00:33:27,977 --> 00:33:29,212
HO!

912
00:33:29,212 --> 00:33:30,213
HO!

913
00:33:30,213 --> 00:33:31,181
HO!

914
00:33:32,549 --> 00:33:34,751
BUT THE FUN QUICKLY
CAME TO A STOP

915
00:33:34,751 --> 00:33:37,220
WHEN LESLIE'S POSTURE AND
PRESENCE FAILED TO HOLD UP.

916
00:33:37,220 --> 00:33:39,456
LESLIE, I THOUGHT YOU WERE
TOO POSE-Y IN YOUR SHOTS.

917
00:33:39,456 --> 00:33:40,757
I DIDN'T SEE YOU
DANCING AT ALL.

918
00:33:40,757 --> 00:33:42,826
AND SHE WAS
SENT HOME.

919
00:33:42,826 --> 00:33:45,962
SARA.

920
00:33:45,962 --> 00:33:47,464
IT'S JUST
THE MAIN FEELING

921
00:33:47,464 --> 00:33:49,365
I'M FEELING RIGHT NOW
IS DISAPPOINTMENT.

922
00:33:49,365 --> 00:33:50,667
I THINK MY PICTURES HAVE BEEN
GOOD, BUT OVERALL,

923
00:33:50,667 --> 00:33:53,470
I HAVEN'T SHOWN THE IMPROVEMENT
THEY WANT TO SEE.

924
00:33:53,470 --> 00:33:54,804
THE FEELING THAT MAYBE
IT WASN'T GOOD ENOUGH,

925
00:33:54,804 --> 00:33:55,972
THAT'S WHAT'S--

926
00:33:55,972 --> 00:33:58,374
THAT'S WHAT'S
DISAPPOINTING.

927
00:33:59,976 --> 00:34:02,345
COMING UP,
JOANIE MAKES A NEW FRIEND.

928
00:34:02,345 --> 00:34:03,713
YOU KNOW WHO'S HOT,
THOUGH?

929
00:34:03,713 --> 00:34:05,482
NIGEL BARKER.

930
00:34:05,482 --> 00:34:07,317
AND LATER,
DANIELLE THE DENTIST

931
00:34:07,317 --> 00:34:09,886
GIVES JADE A TASTE
OF HER OWN MEDICINE.

932
00:34:14,624 --> 00:34:17,292
JADE DOESN'T JUST BRING A
UNIQUE LOOK AND PERSONALITY

933
00:34:17,292 --> 00:34:18,794
TO THE COMPETITION,

934
00:34:18,794 --> 00:34:21,264
SHE ALSO BRINGS
A UNIQUE VOCABULARY.

935
00:34:21,264 --> 00:34:23,299
I ANALYZE EVERYTHING,
EVERYBODY.

936
00:34:23,299 --> 00:34:25,368
I'M JUST
AN "ANALYSTIC" PERSON.

937
00:34:25,368 --> 00:34:26,903
THEY WERE TALKING ABOUT THE--

938
00:34:26,903 --> 00:34:31,307
THE "DECIPHERATION" BETWEEN
CONFIDENCE AND COCKINESS.

939
00:34:31,307 --> 00:34:33,743
I'M DEALING WITH SO MUCH
"TORNNESS."

940
00:34:33,743 --> 00:34:35,245
THE "ARROGANTNESS."

941
00:34:35,245 --> 00:34:36,879
I'M REALLY INTERESTED
IN ACTING,

942
00:34:36,879 --> 00:34:40,450
AND, I'LL PROBABLY "DWELVE" INTO
THIS, YOU KNOW, IN THE FUTURE.

943
00:34:40,450 --> 00:34:42,185
YOU KNOW, I LIKE
MY "BRUNETTENESS,"

944
00:34:42,185 --> 00:34:43,953
BUT THIS IS
AN AWESOME CHANGE

945
00:34:43,953 --> 00:34:46,923
AND I THINK I'M GONNA
STICK WITH IT FOR A WHILE.

946
00:34:46,923 --> 00:34:50,627
SOMETIMES IT'S JUST TOO MUCH
FOR ME TO "WITHHANDLE"-

947
00:34:50,627 --> 00:34:52,595
ACTUALLY, NOT "WITHHANDLE,"
THAT'S NOT A WORD.

948
00:34:52,595 --> 00:34:56,466
YOU KNOW, SOMETIMES IT'S JUST
TOO MUCH FOR THEM TO JUST TAKE.

949
00:34:56,466 --> 00:34:59,401
THE "RELEASEMENT"
OF STRESS.

950
00:34:59,401 --> 00:35:02,372
I DON'T THINK ANYBODY WOULD WANT
TO HEAR ANY "DEROGATORINESS"

951
00:35:02,372 --> 00:35:05,375
AS FAR AS, YOU KNOW, BEING
THE PERSON THAT THEY ARE.

952
00:35:05,375 --> 00:35:08,645
THANK YOU
FOR "CONSIDERATING" ME.

953
00:35:10,780 --> 00:35:13,349
LOTS OF PEOPLE THINK MODELS
ARE BRAINLESS LIVING DOLLS,

954
00:35:13,349 --> 00:35:14,951
SO I DECIDED
TO USE A PHOTO SHOOT

955
00:35:14,951 --> 00:35:17,353
TO MAKE FUN
OF THAT STEREOTYPE.

956
00:35:17,353 --> 00:35:20,790
JOANIE, YOU ARE GOING TO BE
A VENTRILOQUIST'S DOLL.

957
00:35:20,790 --> 00:35:23,626
BROOKE,
YOU'RE GONNA BE A GLAM DOLL.

958
00:35:23,626 --> 00:35:26,896
DANIELLE, YOU ARE GONNA BE
A MARIONETTE, ALL RIGHT?

959
00:35:26,896 --> 00:35:29,265
HOP INTO HAIR AND MAKEUP
AND WE ARE READY TO START.

960
00:35:29,265 --> 00:35:32,202
JAY SAYS I'M GONNA BE
A MARIONETTE DOLL.

961
00:35:32,202 --> 00:35:34,370
WHAT IS THAT WORD
THAT HE JUST SAID?

962
00:35:34,370 --> 00:35:36,306
WHAT IS
A MARIONETTE DOLL?

963
00:35:36,306 --> 00:35:37,740
WHERE'D YOU GROW UP
AGAIN?

964
00:35:37,740 --> 00:35:39,909
UNDER A ROCK?

965
00:35:39,909 --> 00:35:43,546
A MARIONETTE DOLL IS A DOLL
THAT IS CONTROLLED BY STRINGS.

966
00:35:43,546 --> 00:35:45,248
I'M JUST JOKING,
I KNEW THAT.

967
00:35:45,248 --> 00:35:46,850
YOU DID NOT KNOW THAT,
DANIELLE-- NICE TRY!

968
00:35:46,850 --> 00:35:48,218
IF HE WOULD HAVE
JUST TOLD ME,

969
00:35:48,218 --> 00:35:49,686
"DANIELLE, YOU GONNA BE
A DOLL WITH STRINGS,"

970
00:35:49,686 --> 00:35:51,521
I WOULD HAVE BEEN LIKE, "COOL,
I KNOW EXACTLY WHAT THAT IS,"

971
00:35:51,521 --> 00:35:55,225
BUT HE HAD TO GET ALL TECHNICAL
AND SAY A MARIONETTE DOLL.

972
00:35:55,225 --> 00:35:56,960
WHO SAYS THAT?

973
00:35:56,960 --> 00:35:59,596
SO JOANIE, THIS IS GONNA BE
YOUR PUPPET MASTER TODAY,

974
00:35:59,596 --> 00:36:00,430
HIS NAME IS ALEX.

975
00:36:00,430 --> 00:36:01,631
HI!

976
00:36:01,631 --> 00:36:03,366
NICE TO MEET YOU.

977
00:36:03,366 --> 00:36:04,767
LIKE, PRETEND YOU'RE
IN A TRAVELING CIRCUS.

978
00:36:04,767 --> 00:36:07,270
SOME OF THE GIRLS
CAME ALIVE AS LIVING DOLLS.

979
00:36:07,270 --> 00:36:08,271
YOU'RE LOOKING GOOD.

980
00:36:08,271 --> 00:36:09,639
NICE.

981
00:36:09,639 --> 00:36:10,807
LOOK AT THESE.

982
00:36:15,745 --> 00:36:18,348
BUT BROOKE COULDN'T THINK
OUTSIDE THE BOX.

983
00:36:18,348 --> 00:36:20,550
THERE'S SOMETHING
THAT YOU'RE NOT SURE ABOUT.

984
00:36:20,550 --> 00:36:23,820
I NEED YOU TO WORK ON BEING
COMFORTABLE IN YOUR SKIN.

985
00:36:23,820 --> 00:36:26,789
BROOKE, SHE WILL CRY, 'CAUSE
THAT'S JUST IN HER NATURE.

986
00:36:26,789 --> 00:36:29,492
AND IT'S NOT
THE FIRST TIME.

987
00:36:29,492 --> 00:36:31,561
IT'S NOT
THE SECOND TIME.

988
00:36:31,561 --> 00:36:34,464
IT'S NOT THE THIRD TIME,
IT'S NOT THE FOURTH TIME,

989
00:36:34,464 --> 00:36:35,865
IT'S NOT
THE FIFTH TIME.

990
00:36:35,865 --> 00:36:38,534
BROOKE,
GET IT TOGETHER, GIRL.

991
00:36:38,534 --> 00:36:39,569
(wolf whistle)

992
00:36:41,604 --> 00:36:43,473
MISS J., OH NO!

993
00:36:43,473 --> 00:36:44,841
HE'S CRAZY.

994
00:36:44,841 --> 00:36:46,743
YOU KNOW
WHO'S HOT THOUGH?

995
00:36:46,743 --> 00:36:48,411
NIGEL BARKER.

996
00:36:48,411 --> 00:36:50,213
(laughing)

997
00:36:50,213 --> 00:36:51,614
HE IS HOT.

998
00:36:51,614 --> 00:36:53,650
I THINK I WANNA
TAKE THIS HOME WITH ME.

999
00:36:55,652 --> 00:36:57,420
DESPITE HER UPBEAT
ATTITUDE,

1000
00:36:57,420 --> 00:37:00,423
JOANIE WAS PLAGUED
BY AN INSECURITY.

1001
00:37:05,728 --> 00:37:07,430
SHE'S JUST
SO BEAUTIFUL.

1002
00:37:07,430 --> 00:37:10,466
JOANIE HAS LOTS AND LOTS OF
EXTRA TEETH STACKED ON THE TOP,

1003
00:37:10,466 --> 00:37:12,402
ON THE SIDE OF HER MOUTH.

1004
00:37:12,402 --> 00:37:16,339
HER FRONT TOOTH IS KIND OF
CROOKED OVER HER OTHER TOOTH.

1005
00:37:16,339 --> 00:37:18,975
I KNOW PEOPLE ARE GONNA TURN ME
DOWN BECAUSE OF IT, YOU KNOW?

1006
00:37:18,975 --> 00:37:19,742
BUT WHATEVER.

1007
00:37:20,810 --> 00:37:22,912
BUT JOANIE'S DAYS OF BEING
SELF-CONSCIOUS WERE OVER

1008
00:37:22,912 --> 00:37:24,681
WHEN I SENT HER
AND ALL THE GIRLS

1009
00:37:24,681 --> 00:37:26,416
TO GET THEIR SMILES
PERFECTED.

1010
00:37:26,416 --> 00:37:27,884
WE'RE GONNA REMOVE
THESE FOUR.

1011
00:37:27,884 --> 00:37:28,885
TODAY?

1012
00:37:28,885 --> 00:37:30,853
WE'RE GONNA
REMOVE 'EM TODAY.

1013
00:37:30,853 --> 00:37:32,188
LET'S GET THIS
ON YOU HERE.

1014
00:37:32,188 --> 00:37:33,356
WE'LL GET
STARTED.

1015
00:37:41,331 --> 00:37:43,232
WOW, DUDE.

1016
00:37:43,232 --> 00:37:44,600
OH, GOD!

1017
00:37:44,600 --> 00:37:45,802
THANK GOD.

1018
00:37:45,802 --> 00:37:47,337
I FELT
THAT ONE, DUDE.

1019
00:37:47,337 --> 00:37:48,938
ARE MY TEETH
THAT LONG?

1020
00:37:48,938 --> 00:37:50,373
LOOK AT
THAT TOOTH.

1021
00:37:50,373 --> 00:37:51,774
HOLY CRAP,
CAN I HOLD IT?

1022
00:37:51,774 --> 00:37:53,309
YEAH!

1023
00:37:53,309 --> 00:37:54,510
LOOK HOW BIG
THAT IS, JOANIE.

1024
00:37:54,510 --> 00:37:56,446
JOANIE GOT
FOUR TEETH PULLED OUT

1025
00:37:56,446 --> 00:37:59,515
AND I SAW THEM AND THEY LOOKED
LIKE DINOSAUR TEETH.

1026
00:37:59,515 --> 00:38:00,550
I WAS LIKE,
DAMN.

1027
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:02,819
I CAN'T BELIEVE
THIS IS HAPPENING!

1028
00:38:02,819 --> 00:38:05,388
DANIELLE GAVE JOANIE
MORAL SUPPORT

1029
00:38:05,388 --> 00:38:09,726
AND A LITTLE HANDS-ON TREATMENT
FOR EVERYONE ELSE.

1030
00:38:09,726 --> 00:38:12,261
I WAS AT THE DENTIST OFFICE
AND GOT A LITTLE BORED.

1031
00:38:12,261 --> 00:38:13,863
I MEAN, WE WERE IN THERE
FOR HOURS.

1032
00:38:13,863 --> 00:38:15,531
JADE IS JUST
STRAPPED DOWN.

1033
00:38:15,531 --> 00:38:17,734
SHE GOT THIS THING
JAMMED IN HER MOUTH,

1034
00:38:17,734 --> 00:38:20,503
I'M LIKE, "YEAH,
YOU VULNERABLE RIGHT NOW."

1035
00:38:25,641 --> 00:38:27,310
I SUCTIONED HER HEAD
REAL GOOD.

1036
00:38:28,945 --> 00:38:31,314
SHE HAD A LITTLE PERSPIRATION
UP THERE,

1037
00:38:31,314 --> 00:38:33,449
SO I WANTED TO SUCK UP
THEM SWEAT BEADS.

1038
00:38:33,449 --> 00:38:34,717
BAM, BAM!

1039
00:38:34,717 --> 00:38:36,552
I HELPED
A SISTER OUT.

1040
00:38:36,552 --> 00:38:38,254
YOU WANT ME TO GET THAT
PERSPIRATION RIGHT THERE?

1041
00:38:38,254 --> 00:38:39,322
NO?

1042
00:38:39,322 --> 00:38:40,623
OKAY.

1043
00:38:40,623 --> 00:38:41,758
ARE YOU
A LICENSED PROFESSIONAL?

1044
00:38:41,758 --> 00:38:42,859
(record scratching)

1045
00:38:42,859 --> 00:38:43,860
(bell dinging)

1046
00:38:43,860 --> 00:38:45,728
I AIN'T
BREAK IT.

1047
00:38:45,728 --> 00:38:47,830
I JUST STUCK IT
TO HER FOREHEAD...

1048
00:38:47,830 --> 00:38:50,533
A COUPLE TIMES.

1049
00:38:50,533 --> 00:38:53,403
BUT JOANIE CAME AWAY
WITH THE BIGGEST SMILE OF ALL.

1050
00:38:53,403 --> 00:38:54,837
WE'RE ALL DONE.

1051
00:38:54,837 --> 00:38:57,473
LOOK WHAT
YOU GOT NOW.

1052
00:38:57,473 --> 00:38:59,475
OH, MY GOODNESS!

1053
00:38:59,475 --> 00:39:01,377
WOW,
THANK YOU!

1054
00:39:01,377 --> 00:39:03,613
MY PLEASURE,
MY PLEASURE.

1055
00:39:03,613 --> 00:39:06,749
BUT FOR BROOKE, THE SMILES
QUICKLY FADED IN JUDGING.

1056
00:39:06,749 --> 00:39:09,218
THIS IS SO NOT DOLL-LIKE,
REALLY, FOR ME.

1057
00:39:09,218 --> 00:39:11,554
THE ESSENCE OF BROOKE,
THAT'S ALL WE WANT

1058
00:39:11,554 --> 00:39:13,523
AND YOU HAVEN'T DELIVERED THAT
TO US IN PHOTOGRAPHS YET.

1059
00:39:13,523 --> 00:39:16,559
AND SHE BECAME OUR SEVENTH GIRL
ELIMINATED.

1060
00:39:16,559 --> 00:39:17,894
NO MORE CHANCES,
BROOKE.

1061
00:39:17,894 --> 00:39:20,430
I PUT SO MUCH PRESSURE
ON MYSELF TO DO SO WELL

1062
00:39:20,430 --> 00:39:23,332
THAT IT RESTRICTED ME,
I THINK, IN SOME WAYS.

1063
00:39:23,332 --> 00:39:24,934
I KNEW THAT I WAS GOING TO BE
THE ONE WHO WAS GOING HOME.

1064
00:39:27,904 --> 00:39:30,973
EVERY CYCLE, "AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL" GOES INTERNATIONAL

1065
00:39:30,973 --> 00:39:33,776
TO GIVE THE GIRLS
A MORE GLOBAL EXPERIENCE.

1066
00:39:33,776 --> 00:39:36,546
SO WHERE IN THE WORLD DID
"TOP MODEL" GO THIS TIME?

1067
00:39:36,546 --> 00:39:37,547
THAILAND!

1068
00:39:37,547 --> 00:39:40,550
(screaming)

1069
00:39:40,550 --> 00:39:43,319
THAILAND,
WHAT?

1070
00:39:43,319 --> 00:39:44,787
THAILAND!

1071
00:39:44,787 --> 00:39:46,556
THAT'S AROUND
THE WORLD.

1072
00:39:46,556 --> 00:39:48,758
SOME OF THE GIRLS WERE ALREADY
FEELING THE CULTURE SHOCK.

1073
00:39:55,798 --> 00:39:57,366
IT'S A WHOLE NEW WORLD.

1074
00:39:57,366 --> 00:39:58,768
LIKE WE'RE
A MAGIC CARPET.

1075
00:39:58,768 --> 00:40:00,369
GO OVER THERE
AND TURN IT OUT.

1076
00:40:00,369 --> 00:40:01,637
THAILAND.

1077
00:40:01,637 --> 00:40:02,472
THAILAND, BABY,
WHAT?

1078
00:40:02,472 --> 00:40:03,473
THAILAND.

1079
00:40:03,473 --> 00:40:06,309
♪♪♪

1080
00:40:06,309 --> 00:40:08,277
I CAN'T WAIT
TO JUST ARRIVE IN THAILAND.

1081
00:40:08,277 --> 00:40:09,679
IT'S JUST UNREALISTIC TO ME
RIGHT NOW.

1082
00:40:09,679 --> 00:40:11,280
MAN, I--

1083
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:12,648
THIS IS WHY I GET NERVOUS
GOING TO AIRPORTS.

1084
00:40:12,648 --> 00:40:14,383
ALWAYS GOTTA
TAKE OFF YOUR--

1085
00:40:14,383 --> 00:40:16,486
LIKE, LOOK AT ME, I ALWAYS HAVE
TO TAKE OFF EVERYTHING,

1086
00:40:16,486 --> 00:40:17,753
MY BANGLES,
MY EARRINGS.

1087
00:40:17,753 --> 00:40:19,355
MY BOOTS-- I'M LIKE,
LOOK AT ME, MAN.

1088
00:40:19,355 --> 00:40:19,889
LIKE, WHAT, WHAT?

1089
00:40:26,696 --> 00:40:27,697
WE JUST GOT
TO THAILAND,

1090
00:40:27,697 --> 00:40:31,334
IT WAS A 21-HOUR FLIGHT
AND WE--

1091
00:40:31,334 --> 00:40:34,704
EVEN THOUGH WE'RE ALL TIRED
AND EXHAUSTED,

1092
00:40:34,704 --> 00:40:37,306
I'M EXTREMELY
EXCITED.

1093
00:40:37,306 --> 00:40:39,342
BUT THEIR FIRST PHOTO SHOOT
IN THAILAND

1094
00:40:39,342 --> 00:40:41,978
WOULD TURN THE COMPETITION
ON ITS HEAD.

1095
00:40:41,978 --> 00:40:43,513
SO YOU GIRLS
ARE GONNA BE MERMAIDS

1096
00:40:43,513 --> 00:40:45,214
BEING PULLED OUT
OF THE WATER,

1097
00:40:45,214 --> 00:40:47,717
HOISTED UP IN A NET,
KIND OF ON YOUR SIDE

1098
00:40:47,717 --> 00:40:50,820
WITH A FISHTAIL
AND EVERYTHING.

1099
00:40:50,820 --> 00:40:52,922
SOME GIRLS WERE
THE CATCH OF THE DAY.

1100
00:40:52,922 --> 00:40:54,490
STRAIGHTEN
YOUR LEG.

1101
00:40:54,490 --> 00:40:55,825
AND I NEED YOU
TO BE REALLY FEMININE

1102
00:40:55,825 --> 00:40:57,360
ABOUT YOUR ARM
MOVEMENTS.

1103
00:40:57,360 --> 00:40:58,494
ANY SUGGESTIONS?

1104
00:40:58,494 --> 00:40:59,662
NO, I JUST--

1105
00:40:59,662 --> 00:41:03,966
KEEP
THE VARIETY UP.

1106
00:41:03,966 --> 00:41:05,601
THAT'S A PRETTY ONE,
DANIELLE,

1107
00:41:05,601 --> 00:41:08,271
I LIKE HOW
YOU'RE USING YOUR HANDS.

1108
00:41:08,271 --> 00:41:11,240
YES, OH, DO THAT, DO THAT,
DO THAT, IT'S PRETTY.

1109
00:41:11,240 --> 00:41:12,675
WHEN DID YOU LEARN
HOW TO BECOME SOFT?

1110
00:41:12,675 --> 00:41:13,876
I'M LISTENING.

1111
00:41:13,876 --> 00:41:15,578
I'M WATCHING
AND I'M LEARNING.

1112
00:41:15,578 --> 00:41:17,280
OH, OKAY.

1113
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:20,183
KEEP CHANGING UP YOUR HANDS,
FURONDA.

1114
00:41:20,183 --> 00:41:22,919
WHILE OTHERS WERE JUST
LEFT OUT TO DRY.

1115
00:41:22,919 --> 00:41:24,453
THIS HARNESS
THAT THEY HAD ME IN

1116
00:41:24,453 --> 00:41:28,658
IS WAY, WAY TOO TIGHT IN MY
PELVIC AREA, MY WOMANLY SPACE.

1117
00:41:28,658 --> 00:41:30,259
THEY SAID
I LOOKED SCARED,

1118
00:41:30,259 --> 00:41:32,528
BUT I DIDN'T LOOK SCARED,
I LOOKED HURT.

1119
00:41:32,528 --> 00:41:35,331
BUT IT WAS NNENNA
WHO GOT CAUGHT IN A RUT.

1120
00:41:35,331 --> 00:41:37,200
NOW DON'T LET THE PAIN
SHOW IN YOUR FACE.

1121
00:41:37,200 --> 00:41:39,368
DON'T WORRY,
YOU'VE JUST GOT TEN FRAMES.

1122
00:41:39,368 --> 00:41:40,970
CAN I GET A DIFFERENT
FACIAL EXPRESSION?

1123
00:41:40,970 --> 00:41:41,971
I CAN'T.

1124
00:41:43,439 --> 00:41:44,907
I DON'T FEEL
MERMAID HERE.

1125
00:41:44,907 --> 00:41:47,643
YOU JUST REALLY NEED TO BRING UP
SOMETHING DIFFERENT.

1126
00:41:47,643 --> 00:41:49,245
NOT JUST
THE SAME OLD NNENNA.

1127
00:41:49,245 --> 00:41:51,347
SOME OF THE JUDGES
ARE LIKE, "I'M BORED."

1128
00:41:51,347 --> 00:41:53,816
WHAT ELSE IS SHE BRINGING
TO THE TABLE?

1129
00:41:53,816 --> 00:41:58,621
AND THE JUDGES DECIDED
NNENNA'S JOURNEY WAS OVER.

1130
00:41:58,621 --> 00:42:00,690
I'M SURPRISED I'M THE ONE
GOING HOME TONIGHT,

1131
00:42:00,690 --> 00:42:02,825
BUT COMING
INTO THIS COMPETITION,

1132
00:42:02,825 --> 00:42:04,794
THERE ARE
NO CERTAINTIES.

1133
00:42:09,198 --> 00:42:11,667
NOW,
ONLY FIVE GIRLS REMAIN.

1134
00:42:11,667 --> 00:42:14,203
DANIELLE, THE STRIKING
GAP-TOOTHED CHARMER

1135
00:42:14,203 --> 00:42:15,972
FROM LITTLE ROCK,
ARKANSAS.

1136
00:42:15,972 --> 00:42:18,241
JOANIE,
THE SEXY PREACHER'S DAUGHTER

1137
00:42:18,241 --> 00:42:20,209
FROM BEAVER FALLS,
PENNSYLVANIA.

1138
